findings.body:
When `useStateFavicon` unmounts it resets the icon to `/favicon-16x16.png` and friends. Those files are under `ui-v2/public/ico/`, not the public root, so the reset requests return 404. After a user leaves a task run page, the browser tab keeps a broken icon for the rest of the session.

::diff{file="ui-v2/src/hooks/use-state-favicon.ts" lines="55-64"}

::callout{type="warning"}
The default `<link>` tags in `index.html` point at `/ico/favicon-*.png`. The reset paths should match those, not the root.

::suggestion{file="ui-v2/src/hooks/use-state-favicon.ts" lines="55-64"}
		return () => {
			// Reset to default favicon on unmount
			if (colorScheme === "dark") {
				favicon16?.setAttribute("href", "/ico/favicon-16x16-dark.png");
				favicon32?.setAttribute("href", "/ico/favicon-32x32-dark.png");
			} else {
				favicon16?.setAttribute("href", "/ico/favicon-16x16.png");
				favicon32?.setAttribute("href", "/ico/favicon-32x32.png");
			}
		};

`StateType` includes CANCELLING and PAUSED, so `useStateFavicon` sets the icon to `/cancelling.svg` or `/paused.svg`. Neither file is in `ui-v2/public`, so those states produce a 404 and a broken icon. The PR's review checklist says these states "will not update favicon", which is not what the code does. It sets a bad href.

::diff{file="ui-v2/src/hooks/use-state-favicon.ts" lines="49-53"}

Either add the two SVGs, or skip the update for states without an icon (for example, check the set of supported states and only set the href when one exists).

The new Retry Jitter Factor row uses a truthiness check. A jitter factor of `0` is a valid value (no jitter), and it's typed `number | null` in `ui-v2/src/api/prefect.ts`. With this change, `0` shows "None", which looks like the value is missing. The old code showed `0` when the value was not null or undefined.

::diff{file="ui-v2/src/components/task-runs/task-run-details/task-run-details.tsx" lines="176-183"}

Use a null and undefined check, the same way the Estimated Run Time and Duration rows do.

The PR description lists Run Count among the fields that now show "None" when empty. The code uses `taskRun.run_count || 0`, so a null run count renders as `0`. The description and the code disagree. A reviewer checking parity with Vue will see a different empty state.

::diff{file="ui-v2/src/components/task-runs/task-run-details/task-run-details.tsx" lines="86-89"}

If "None" is the intent, use the same null check as the other rows. If `0` is intended, update the description.

The Flow Run row used to require both `flow_run_name` and `flow_run_id`. It now only checks `flow_run_id`. If the id is set but the name is null, the link renders with no visible text, so it's an invisible, unlabeled link.

::diff{file="ui-v2/src/components/task-runs/task-run-details/task-run-details.tsx" lines="45-58"}

Either keep the name check in the condition, or fall back to the id as the link text.
